{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAsMov2q7r6U9r3kLBjQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night; it fails, and then the failure message never gets sent. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`, and every run wrote the same two lines to `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`:\n\n1. **`Not logged in · Please run /login`**: the plist only sets `PATH`. Without `USER`, `claude` can't find its login in the keychain and quits straight away.\n2. **`read-only variable: status`**: in zsh, `status` is a built-in you can't assign to. `status=$?` on line 19 kills the script right there, before it reaches the line that sends the failure message.\n\n**Fixes:**\n- **Plist:** added `USER`, `HOME` and `LANG` to the environment.\n- **Script:**\n  - `status` is now `rc`.\n  - The prompt goes in through stdin instead of as an argument.\n  - Each run logs its exit code and how long it took.\n  - A run that exits 0 but writes an empty file now counts as a failure.\n  - The summary is cut at 300 characters instead of 300 bytes. Cutting by bytes could break a non-English character in half, and Telegram rejects that.\n  - If sending the message fails, that now goes to the error log.\n- **`notify.sh`:** curl now uses `-f` (plus 2 retries), so an error from Telegram counts as a failure instead of passing silently.\n\nI tested the script with a fake `claude` and a fake notifier. A \"Not logged in\" failure now sends the FAILED message and exits 1, and a successful run sends the summary. Nothing has been tested against real launchd, the real `claude` or Telegram.\n\nOn your Mac, unload the job, load it again and kick it off once (the commands are in `ANSWER.md`). Then check that a message arrives and the output file has a real review in it. If it still says \"Not logged in\", the fallback is to run `claude setup-token` and put the token in the plist as `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`.\n\nThe plist values (`/Users/vk`, `USER=vk`) follow the paths in your snapshot, so change them if your real username is different."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1498,"cache_read_input_tokens":29928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1498},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a0ad04f-3f18-42c5-a87a-e0825374b1bf","uuid":"7abe73e4-e7d2-4452-bd04-6b70eeba7cf9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:15:45.800Z","request_id":"req_011CgAsModfu3PGwyrEc6pHu"}
